id: pm-ap7ilf
title: MCP create drops advertised metadata outside its small top-level allowlist
description: "Independent stateless stdio reproduction while addressing pm-gh1538: pm_create advertises deadline but ignores a top-level deadline=2026-11-01 with title/type and options.createMode=progressive, returns success and creates an item with no deadline. The same shared SDK hoist path also omits explicit create id and other canonical metadata. Extend canonical parameter normalization and atomic malformed-value preflight to create while preserving native SDK input admission, custom fields, nested aliases and template/type resolution."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-21T23:10:30.182Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-22T04:40:10.312Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-22T04:40:09.546Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-22T04:40:09.546Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 90
acceptance_criteria: Persist schema-advertised create metadata including explicit id and deadline; Explicit nested values and equivalent aliases retain precedence; Malformed typed fields refuse before creating any item or history; Public MCP and SDK compatibility plus packed npm and Bun consumers pass
parent: pm-5k4v
risk: medium
confidence: 95
severity: medium
resolution: "Create uses canonical SDK metadata contracts, refuses malformed inputs atomically, retains nested/custom/false/completion metadata and exposes a documented runtime-field option lookup helper."
expected_result: "Persist declared create metadata, refuse malformed values before durable writes, and document the public helper contract and precedence for package authors."
actual_result: "Durable integration tests preserve id, deadline, custom fields, regression=false and supplied completion metadata; invalid requests leave item/history bytes identical. Full coverage passes10982 tests at100percent; packed Node/Bun consumers and complete static gates pass. The final TSDoc-only correction passes build,33 focused tests, docstring/export/public-surface and documentation-link checks with zero signature changes."
